<title>GERMANY: Siemens unit plans to buy Amana - report.</title>
<headline>Siemens unit plans to buy Amana - report.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bosch-Siemens Hausgeraete (BSGH), a unit of German industrial group Siemens AG, plans to buy U.S. home appliances maker Amana from its parent Raytheon, the news magazine Der Spiegel reported.</p>
<p>The purchase price was said to be $700 million, Spiegel said, adding BSGH management had already approved the plan.</p>
<p>The purchase would put Siemens among the world's leading makers of stoves and refrigerators. Raytheon hopes to focus more on its defence business, the magazine said.</p>
<p>Siemens officials were unavailable for comment.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
